        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Product Goals, KPIs, and Measurement</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Measurable product goals provide teams with a way to understand
                    whether their efforts are producing the expected results. Key
                    performance indicators should be selected based on the nature of the
                    product, business model, customer journey, and strategic objectives.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Customer Metrics</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Customer satisfaction, retention, adoption, engagement, and feedback
                    can help determine whether the product is delivering meaningful value
                    to its target users.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Product Metrics</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Product usage, feature adoption, activation, conversion, and
                    engagement metrics provide insight into how customers interact with
                    the product.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Business Metrics</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Revenue, growth, customer acquisition, cost efficiency, and other
                    business indicators can help determine whether product goals are
                    contributing to organizational performance.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Operational Metrics</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Delivery efficiency, product quality, support requirements, and
                    operational performance can help teams identify areas where product
                    processes require improvement.
                </p>
            </div>

